    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-057 — `parent_content_height` threading + `%` height/max-height.** One commit. **Docs follow after merge.**\n\nCloses ADR-039's and ADR-053's explicit `%` deferrals. Unblocks ADR-058's `translateY` chain.\n\n## The verified delta\n\n**669 / 2562 all pass** (was 663 / 2550). **6 new tests prove every layer:**\n\n| Test | Proves |\n|---|---|\n| `html height:100%` → 600 | `<html>` special case fires (uses `viewport_h`) |\n| `html,body height:100%` chains → 600 | Full `html→body→x` propagation |\n| `height:50%` on fixed 200px parent → 100 | `%` resolves against explicit parent height |\n| `height:50%` on auto parent → skips | **CSS spec correctness** — auto parent gives 0 |\n| `max-height:30%` on fixed parent → 60 | Guard removal + `parse_length_for_height` works |\n| `min-height:50%` on fixed parent → 100 | Same |\n\n**Zero existing test changes.** The test at `test_box_model.cpp:109` still passes unchanged — its `run()` uses default `viewport_height=0`, so `%` correctly resolves to 0 in that setup.\n\n## What shipped\n\n### `LengthContext` + new parser\n\n```cpp\nstruct LengthContext {\n    float parent_content_width = 0.0f;      // pre-existing\n    float parent_content_height = 0.0f;     // ADR-057\n    // ...\n};\n```\n\n`parse_length_for_height(sv, ctx)`: trailing `%` resolves against `ctx.parent_content_height`; non-% delegates to `parse_length`.\n\n### `<html>` / `<body>` special case\n\n`<html>`'s containing block is the **initial containing block = viewport** (CSS spec). So `html { height: 100% }` — the universal CSS reset — resolves against `viewport_h`, not `parent_content_height`. `<body>` then gets `<html>`'s resolved height as its parent.\n\n**Without this special case, `html, body { height: 100% }` would still skip**, defeating the whole cycle for the most common real-world case.\n\n### 8 recursive call sites updated\n\n| Line | Context |\n|---|---|\n| 1064 | Block child, x=0 y=0 |\n| 1109 | Block child, x=cursor_x y=cursor_y |\n| 1193 | Narrow-width child |\n| 1278 | Flex natural-size probe |\n| 1397 | Inline fragment |\n| 1563 | Grid cell |\n| 1677 | Absolute positioned |\n| 2140 | Root entry from `layout()` |\n\nEach passes `own_content_height` (computed once per element via `own_declared_content_height()` helper).\n\n### 3 skip guards removed\n\n| Site | Line | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `height:` | 1835 | `find('%') == npos` | uses `parse_length_for_height` |\n| `min-height:` | 1848 | same | same |\n| `max-height:` | 1857 | same | same |\n\n### Definition-body signatures (caught during build)\n\nFirst attempt updated `.hpp` declarations but missed `.cpp` definition bodies → `'parent_content_height' was not declared` at the root call. Fix: add the param to `layout()` and `layout_with_pseudo()` definitions, pass through. **Same class of split-declaration bug as ADR-051's `parse_operand` discovery.**\n\n## The circularity constraint (honest)\n\n`layout_element` recurses into children first, then applies its own explicit `height:`. So **auto-height parents don't know their own content height during child layout.**\n\n**CSS spec**: child `%` height on auto parent → auto (skip). **This is correct behavior, not a limitation.** Chromium/Firefox/WebKit all do this.\n\n**Consequence**: the visible delta is narrower than the deferral list suggests. `%` heights on auto-height parents still skip. Only `%` on **fixed-height** parents resolve.\n\n## What this PR does NOT do\n\n- **Magnifier still ~10px high.** `top: 50%` + `translateY(-50%)` deferred to ADR-058. Shipping `top: 50%` alone moves the magnifier from y=7 to y=28 (worse).\n- **Auto-height parents still skip `%`** — CSS spec.\n- **`%` width, `%` margin, `%` padding** — untouched (already work against `parent_content_width`).\n\n## The magnifier chain (after ADR-057)\n\n| Layer | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `background-image` renders | ✅ ADR-056 |\n| `parent_content_height` available | ✅ **ADR-057 (this PR)** |\n| `top: 50%` resolves | ⏸ ADR-058 |\n| `translateY(-50%)` centers | ⏸ ADR-058 |\n\nOne step closer, one step to go.\n\n## Test count\n\n- 663 → 669 cases (+6)\n- 2550 → 2562 assertions (+12)\n- Zero existing tests changed\n\nRefs #252\n",
